From 33cf0e5cf29581599ef4220cc5b5a19422ad11bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:53:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] FEXInterpreter: turn the code cache off when SMC store
 backpatching is on

CodeBufferManager::TryAllocateAuxMemory refuses every backpatch stub while
EnableCodeCachingWIP is set, because the cache replays the code buffer and
stubs do not survive that. The syscall handler only refuses backpatching when
the cache also *writes* (CodeCacheWriteEnabled). With the cache enabled in its
load-only scope (CodeCacheScope=off, the default scope), backpatching was
reported as enabled and then silently placed no stub at all.

Resolve the conflict once, right after the config is loaded: an explicit
FEX_SMCSTOREBACKPATCH wins and EnableCodeCachingWIP is forced off before
anything reads it. The syscall handler's "incompatible with code cache
writing" refusal is left in place; it is no longer reachable from the
interpreter.

Evidence (static x86-64 program, FEX_SMCSTOREBACKPATCH=1
FEX_SMCSTOREEMULATION=1 FEX_SMCCHECKS=mtrack FEX_ENABLECODECACHINGWIP=1,
log to stderr):
  before: "SMC store backpatching enabled" together with
          "exit-RIP constants are FIXED width ... (code caching on ...)",
          i.e. a backpatcher whose every stub allocation is refused;
  after:  "SMC store backpatching enabled" with "(code caching off ...)".

Only SMCStoreBackpatch is gated here. POWERarm also turns the cache off for
SMCSemanticPatch, SMCLazyInval, SMCCheapTier and SMCStoreEmulation, whose
per-block state its cache format does not store; whether that holds for this
tree's cache format is left to review.

Ported from POWERarm 60bc2ddbc (SMC part only).
---
 Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp b/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp
index e013bbac1..5107c2460 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/FEXInterpreter.cpp
@@ -485,6 +485,18 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv, char** const envp) {
   FEXCore::Config::ReloadMetaLayer();
   FEXCore::Config::Set(FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_INTERPRETER_INSTALLED, InterpreterInstalled ? "1" : "0");
 
+  // SMC store backpatching and the code cache do not mix: the cache replays the
+  // code buffer, and backpatch stubs (absolute helper addresses, PC-relative
+  // branches to store sites) do not survive that, so
+  // CodeBufferManager::TryAllocateAuxMemory refuses every stub while
+  // EnableCodeCachingWIP is set. With the cache only loading (CodeCacheScope
+  // off) the syscall handler still enabled backpatching, which then silently
+  // placed no stub at all. The explicit SMC mode wins: turn the cache off here,
+  // before anything has read the option.
+  if (FEXCore::Config::Get_SMCSTOREBACKPATCH() && FEXCore::Config::Get_ENABLECODECACHINGWIP()) {
+    FEXCore::Config::Set(FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_ENABLECODECACHINGWIP, "0");
+  }
+
   // Host-page-size gate (64K port). Config is loaded and merged, and nothing
   // downstream exists yet: no context (CreateNewContext below caches SMCChecks
   // at construction, which is why degrade-mode forcing has to happen HERE), no
